==Battleground==
*1 [[Cala Maria]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[J.K. Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss.
*When the base reaches 98% HP:
**1 [[Othom]] spawns as the boss.
*When the base reaches 97% HP:
**1 [[Winged Pigge]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
This stage simply requires four different variants of chip damage for the traits seen in the stage, such as Ramen Cat for Cala Maria and Winged Pigge. [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] can be primarily used to trigger boss waves due to their low damage. Just make sure to be cautious of using units like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] that can deal large chunks of damage to the base. Higher difficulties may require [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-control units]] due to the high damage the enemies can dish out.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: A very good meatshield here as his [[Resistant|resistance]] to [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] allows him to tank many hits from the Cala Maria. His high base heath allows him to take hits from even J.K. Bun Bun.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Deals [[Massive Damage|massive]] amounts of damage to the J.K. Bun Bun and has great base stats, allowing him to also help with the Othom.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: '''Can''' be used to deal high amounts of damage, but this adds the risk of him hitting the base and spawning all 3 bosses at once. If you have his [[Explosion]] [[Talents|Talent]], he is more efficient as his Explosion might severely damage the bosses on base hit.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Most of the [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] units work well here, as they're designed to deal with traited enemies.
*[[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Chronos the Almighty]]: Can [[Freeze]] all enemies in the stage for a decent amount of time, allowing you to deal significant damage to them.
*[[:Category:Nuker-class Cats|Nukers]] like [[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai DX]] or [[Ushiwakamaru (Legend Rare Cat)|Colossal Benkei]]: A great help, as they are able to annihilate the enemies they target, thus decreasing the amount of threats.

==Trivia==
*"Pulling punches" is an idiom meaning "to hold back", as in restraining oneself when punching or wording a phrase delicately when speaking to avoid giving offense or inciting anger. Pulling punches is indeed encouraged in this stage, as doing so will allow you to fight the bosses one at a time rather than simultaneously.
*Pulled Punch Bout's Japanese name, 寸止め打撃対戦 ''Sundome Dageki Taisen'', is derived from 寸止め ''[[wikipedia:ja:寸止め|sundome]]'' (to stop an action the moment before, or to restrain oneself during a martial arts move to the extent that it does not cause damage), 打撃 ''dageki'' (strike/blow), 対戦 ''taisen'' (competition) and possibly 打撃戦 ''dagekisen'' (a game involving many hits).

